 "note": "Thomas C. Passios Elementary School, identified by its own heading on line 13 ('THOMAS C. PASSIOS ELEMENTARY SCHOOL FACULTY'). Lines 1-7 are the end of the principal's narrative. Lines 8-12 are the Passios School Council for 2002-2003 (a governance body including parents), kept as entries with grade_or_dept 'School Council'; line 11 'Community Representative: open' names no one and is ignored. Line 47 is the 'SPECIAL SERVICES REPORT' section title and line 48 its byline (Elaine E. Blaisdell, Student Services Coordinator), treated as headings; lines 49-50 are that report's narrative and line 51 the page number. Layout: two columns, each a label and a name (Textract x 0.03/0.15 and 0.39/0.57 or similar). The left-column office labels (Principal, Asst. Prin., Adm. Sec., Guidance, Nurse) are titles and go in role_raw; the grade labels (Preschool, Kindergarten, Grade 1-4) and every right-column label (Learning Center, Art, Cafeteria, Custodians ...) are section labels governing the names below them and go in grade_or_dept. A cell printing two names with '/' is two entries. '(Pri.)' after a name is kept in role_raw as printed (it marks the Primary School). Line 17 prints '(TCP)' between the nurses and the right column; kept in the Nurse role. Line 18's Sharron Massie / Rosemary Sullender continue the Nurse block. Honorifics printed before names (Mr., Mrs., Ms., Dr.) are not carried in `name`."
